32	/**
33	 * The client end of a multiplayer world: owns the WebSocket and a REPLICA
34	 * engine the existing renderer/audio/HUD consume unchanged. Outbound, it
35	 * streams the local player's pose at tick rate and routes commands — local
36	 * presentation stays on the replica, gameplay goes to the server (selectSlot
37	 * optimistically does both). Inbound, it applies the server's block journal,
38	 * replays events into the shell's existing event drain, feeds pose buffers
39	 * for ~125 ms-delayed interpolation, and overwrites the local player's
40	 * private state from self-deltas (the server owns your vitals).
